WEBVTT

00:00:01.412 --> 00:00:10.778
Domino's, level one, the wrong trousers, chapter one, happy birthday Chuck.

00:00:10.838 --> 00:00:15.491
It was early in the morning on Wednesday the 12th.

00:00:15.551 --> 00:00:24.176
Grommet the dog sat at the table in the kitchen of the little house at 62 West Wallaby Street and made breakfast.

00:00:24.236 --> 00:00:32.144
Suddenly he remembered something He got up from the table and went to look at the calendar near the door.

00:00:32.204 --> 00:00:36.006
Wednesday the twelfth was his birthday.

00:00:36.066 --> 00:00:39.308
There it was on the calendar in blue pen.

00:00:39.368 --> 00:00:42.020
Gromit's birthday.

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:48.194
Gromit took a pen and put a big blue X through the number twelve.

00:00:48.254 --> 00:00:57.204
It's my birthday today and my friend Wallace is sleeping, he thought, and he felt sad.

00:00:57.264 --> 00:00:59.728
Wallace wasn't a dog.

00:00:59.788 --> 00:01:06.470
He was a man, and Gromit lived with him at 62 West Wallaby Street.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:09.071
Gromit looked at his watch.

00:01:09.131 --> 00:01:11.442
It was nine o'clock.

00:01:11.502 --> 00:01:15.403
Just then he heard a noise at the front door.

00:01:15.463 --> 00:01:16.754
There!

00:01:16.814 --> 00:01:19.915
That's the postman, he thought.

00:01:19.975 --> 00:01:24.106
Perhaps I'm going to get some birthday cards this morning.

00:01:24.166 --> 00:01:26.375
Let's go and see.

00:01:26.435 --> 00:01:34.238
There were six letters by the front door when Gromit arrived there, and he looked at all of them carefully.

00:01:34.298 --> 00:01:40.822
Most of them were letters for Wallace, letters in brown envelopes asking for money.

00:01:40.882 --> 00:01:45.896
But there was one envelope, a green one, for Gromit.

00:01:45.956 --> 00:01:51.320
With all six letters in his mouth, Gromit ran back to the kitchen.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:57.814
Suddenly a toy train shot out in front of him, He stopped for a minute.

00:01:57.874 --> 00:02:03.595
The train went past, and then he ran on, back to the breakfast table.

00:02:03.655 --> 00:02:10.628
There were lots of different machines in Wallace and Gromit's house in West Wallaby Street.

00:02:10.688 --> 00:02:17.200
Back in the kitchen, Gromit sat down at the table and opened the green envelope.

00:02:17.260 --> 00:02:26.990
It was a birthday card with a picture of a smiling dog on the front And when he opened it, it played, Happy Birthday to you!"

00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:32.454
Grommet put the card on the table, and looked at it sadly.

00:02:32.514 --> 00:02:36.858
Only one birthday card on his birthday.

00:02:36.918 --> 00:02:43.141
Just then, a red light over his head began to go on and off.

00:02:43.201 --> 00:02:46.499
Upstairs Wallace was in bed.

00:02:46.559 --> 00:02:50.268
there was a red button next to his bed.

00:02:50.328 --> 00:02:53.290
It said breakfast on it.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:56.373
Wallace hit it again and again.

00:02:56.433 --> 00:03:00.967
Breakfast said the red light in the kitchen over Gromit's head.

00:03:01.027 --> 00:03:06.162
Down in the kitchen Gromit moved a lever behind his chair.

00:03:06.222 --> 00:03:11.942
At once, up in Wallace's room, the head of the bed moved up.

00:03:12.002 --> 00:03:17.501
At the same time a door opened in the floor at the foot of the bed.

00:03:17.561 --> 00:03:21.494
The table in the kitchen was right under this door.

00:03:21.554 --> 00:03:26.766
Suddenly Wallace shot out of bed crying, grommet!

00:03:26.826 --> 00:03:35.660
He shot down through the door in the floor and was soon downstairs, sitting in his chair at the kitchen table.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:45.537
Oh, well, Gromit, my getting up in the morning machine worked well, said Wallace, and he began to eat his breakfast.

00:03:45.596 --> 00:03:49.900
But perhaps I can make it work better.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:54.262
I hit the chair very fast that time, ouch!

00:03:54.322 --> 00:03:58.706
Cracking breakfast, Gromit, he went on.

00:03:58.766 --> 00:04:03.008
Gromit read his newspaper and said nothing.

00:04:03.068 --> 00:04:05.438
Any letters today?"

00:04:05.498 --> 00:04:06.930
asked Wallace.

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:09.802
Gromit gave him his letters.

00:04:09.862 --> 00:04:17.838
Wallace opened the first brown envelope and took out a very long letter asking him for lots of money.

00:04:17.897 --> 00:04:19.839
Oh, dear!

00:04:19.899 --> 00:04:23.542
said Wallace, looking at the long letter carefully.

00:04:23.602 --> 00:04:27.736
He looked at all the brown envelopes in his hand.

00:04:27.796 --> 00:04:32.053
We must be more careful with money, Gromit!

00:04:32.113 --> 00:04:35.760
A grommet put his birthday card on the table.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:39.652
It played happy birthday slowly and sadly.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:43.814
But Wallace wasn't interested in birthday cards just then.

00:04:43.874 --> 00:04:47.117
Wallace went to look in his money-box.

00:04:47.176 --> 00:04:50.758
There was only thirty pens in it.

00:04:50.818 --> 00:04:54.460
Look at that, he said.

00:04:54.520 --> 00:04:57.348
And those presents weren't cheap.

00:04:57.408 --> 00:05:01.016
He put his hand over his mouth and looked at Gromit.

00:05:01.076 --> 00:05:06.189
Oh, no, he didn't want Gromit to know about his presence just then.

00:05:06.248 --> 00:05:11.011
Gromit looked at Wallace, and his ears went up excitedly.

00:05:11.071 --> 00:05:17.304
Perhaps I'm going to get something more for my birthday, he thought.

00:05:17.364 --> 00:05:22.436
Well, Gromit, what's on the 905 train?

00:05:22.496 --> 00:05:23.776
said Wallace.

00:05:23.836 --> 00:05:25.157
Oh, look!

00:05:25.217 --> 00:05:27.450
Here it comes now!

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:33.936
Wallace's little toy train came through the kitchen door and shot past the table.

00:05:33.996 --> 00:05:37.368
Quickly, Wallace took a little present of it.

00:05:37.428 --> 00:05:38.858
What's this?

00:05:38.918 --> 00:05:43.230
He said, and he put the present on the table in front of Gromit.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:46.062
Happy birthday, Chuck!

00:05:46.122 --> 00:05:49.864
Gromit quickly opened his birthday present.

00:05:49.924 --> 00:05:53.054
It was a red dog collar and lead.

00:05:53.114 --> 00:05:56.594
You wanted a collar, said Wallace laughing.

00:05:56.654 --> 00:05:59.306
Here, let's put it on you."

00:05:59.366 --> 00:06:02.910
Wallace helped Gromit to put on his collar.

00:06:02.970 --> 00:06:07.704
Now people can see you come from a good home, he said.

00:06:07.763 --> 00:06:09.586
But that isn't all.

00:06:09.645 --> 00:06:11.677
Come and look in here.

00:06:11.697 --> 00:06:15.460
A Gromit went into the front room.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.343
Something stood there in the dark.

00:06:18.403 --> 00:06:20.704
A new machine, perhaps.

00:06:20.763 --> 00:06:26.006
It began to make a noise, and it came out from behind the door.

00:06:26.066 --> 00:06:30.220
It was a big, walking present.

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:35.514
It walked nearer and nearer to Gromit on its two big legs.

00:06:35.573 --> 00:06:38.366
Gromit felt very afraid.

00:06:38.426 --> 00:06:44.381
Suddenly the thing stopped, and Gromit saw a small card on the front of it.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:48.876
To Gromit, love Wallace, said the card.

00:06:48.936 --> 00:06:54.694
because grommet was afraid, in the end Wallace opened this second present.

00:06:54.754 --> 00:06:56.826
But what was it?

00:06:56.886 --> 00:07:00.670
Green and black trousers?

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:06.967
Yes, but they were trousers with blue buttons and red levers.

00:07:07.026 --> 00:07:10.480
There, techno trousers!

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:16.088
said Wallace.

00:07:16.148 --> 00:07:34.542
Chapter 2 Room for Rent I think you're going to like these techno trousers, Wallace said.

00:07:34.602 --> 00:07:41.207
He put one end of Gromit's new lead on his collar and the other end on the trousers.

00:07:41.267 --> 00:07:46.440
Then he hit some blue buttons and moved some red levers.

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:48.560
Time for a walk!

00:07:48.620 --> 00:07:50.020
Ten?

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:51.011
No!

00:07:51.071 --> 00:07:53.872
Twenty minutes, he said.

00:07:53.932 --> 00:07:55.793
Now what's happening?

00:07:55.853 --> 00:07:57.214
Thought Gromit.

00:07:57.273 --> 00:08:06.558
Suddenly the techno-trousers began walking out of the door, and Gromit, in his collar and lead, went sadly with them.

00:08:06.618 --> 00:08:09.288
Have a nice walk, Gromit!

00:08:09.348 --> 00:08:11.390
Wallace laughed.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:14.360
There was a sign in the park.

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:18.138
All dogs on a lead, it said.

00:08:18.198 --> 00:08:23.327
But when Grommet arrived, he didn't have his new lead on.

00:08:23.387 --> 00:08:25.228
Where was it?

00:08:25.288 --> 00:08:27.940
On a toy dog!

00:08:27.999 --> 00:08:37.054
So in the end Grommet played happily in the park, and the techno-trousers took the toy dog for a walk.

00:08:37.114 --> 00:08:43.687
At home, in 62 West Wallaby Street, Wallace sat in the kitchen.

00:08:43.747 --> 00:08:48.910
He had all the letters asking for money on the table in front of him.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:51.000
"'It's no good.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:54.692
We need some more money,' he said.

00:08:54.752 --> 00:08:59.583
He wrote out a sign and put it in the front window of the house.

00:08:59.603 --> 00:09:04.265
"'Spare room for rent,' it said.

00:09:04.325 --> 00:09:09.336
Grommet saw the sign when he came back from the park.

00:09:09.396 --> 00:09:14.368
Later that day, Wallace and Grommet sat in the front room.

00:09:14.388 --> 00:09:17.940
"'Did you have a nice walk, Chuck?'

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.356
asked Wallace.

00:09:19.416 --> 00:09:22.483
How were the techno trousers?"

00:09:22.544 --> 00:09:26.887
Gromit looked at him sadly and said nothing.

00:09:26.946 --> 00:09:30.990
Suddenly they heard a ring at the front door.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:34.632
There's someone at the door, Gromit!

00:09:34.692 --> 00:09:39.636
Wallace quickly got up and went to open the front door.

00:09:39.696 --> 00:09:48.544
Gromit stayed in his chair, but his ears went up and he listened carefully to everything through the open door.

00:09:48.603 --> 00:09:51.296
"'Are you here about the room?'

00:09:51.356 --> 00:09:52.727
asked Wallace.

00:09:52.787 --> 00:09:56.508
That's grand coming!'

00:09:56.568 --> 00:10:06.274
The next minute a penguin walked quietly into 62 West Wallaby Street, with a little black bag.

00:10:06.334 --> 00:10:08.555
He went upstairs with Wallace.

00:10:08.575 --> 00:10:12.527
"'I'm asking twenty pounds a week.

00:10:12.587 --> 00:10:16.834
That's with breakfast,' Wallace said to the penguin.

00:10:16.894 --> 00:10:19.720
They walked past Gromit's room.

00:10:19.781 --> 00:10:27.118
It's cheap, because it's a dark room, said Wallace, opening the door to the spare room.

00:10:27.178 --> 00:10:30.240
But we can soon make it nice.

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:37.668
The penguin took one look at the dark and dirty spare room, and ran into Gromit's room.

00:10:37.728 --> 00:10:40.610
No, wait a minute, said Wallace.

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:50.662
You can't But the penguin got up on Gromit's bed, opened his bag, sat back happily, and began listening to the radio.

00:10:50.722 --> 00:10:52.164
Ah, yes!

00:10:52.224 --> 00:10:53.384
Well!

00:10:53.444 --> 00:11:04.042
That's okay then, said Wallace slowly, and he left the penguin in Gromit's room, closed the door, and went downstairs.

00:11:04.102 --> 00:11:12.207
With the penguin now in Gromit's room, Gromit moved into the spare room, It's okay, Grommet.

00:11:12.267 --> 00:11:16.278
We can soon make it nice," said Wallace.

00:11:16.338 --> 00:11:20.739
Of course, they had the techno-trousers to help them.

00:11:20.799 --> 00:11:27.510
The penguin was very, very interested in those when he saw them.

00:11:27.570 --> 00:11:35.592
Grommet couldn't sleep in his bed in the spare room that night because he could hear the penguin's radio.

00:11:35.652 --> 00:11:40.813
He went downstairs but he could hear the radio there, too.

00:11:40.873 --> 00:11:52.366
Angrily he went upstairs again to speak to the penguin, but he couldn't open the door to his room, and there was no answer when he knocked on it.

00:11:52.426 --> 00:12:01.000
In the end Gromit went out sadly into the garden, but he could hear the radio out there, too.

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:05.544
Very late that night the penguin arrived home.

00:12:05.604 --> 00:12:10.688
He went into the house, up to his room and to bed.

00:12:10.748 --> 00:12:15.200
Then the radio stopped and everything went quiet.

00:12:15.260 --> 00:12:26.405
In the garden Gromit put his head in his hands and cried quietly.

00:12:26.465 --> 00:12:44.930
Chapter Three Penguin That's Grand The next day, when Gromit went to the bathroom, there was someone in there.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:46.942
Gromit waited.

00:12:47.002 --> 00:12:49.222
Wallace walked past.

00:12:49.282 --> 00:12:54.434
Good morning Gromit, he said happily, and he went down to breakfast.

00:12:54.494 --> 00:12:57.896
Then the penguin came out of the bathroom.

00:12:57.956 --> 00:13:03.518
Later, when Gromit sat down for breakfast, Wallace put his feet up.

00:13:03.578 --> 00:13:07.004
The penguin quickly brought his slippers to him.

00:13:07.064 --> 00:13:10.952
Thank you very much, Penguin, that's grand!"

00:13:11.012 --> 00:13:14.364
said Wallace, putting his feet into the slippers.

00:13:14.424 --> 00:13:19.178
Gromit usually took Wallace's newspaper when it came in the morning.

00:13:19.238 --> 00:13:25.012
But now the Penguin got to the front door and back with a newspaper before Gromit.

00:13:25.072 --> 00:13:27.404
What do you think of that, Gromit?

00:13:27.464 --> 00:13:28.755
asked Wallace.

00:13:28.815 --> 00:13:31.578
Our new friends a great help!

00:13:31.638 --> 00:13:33.058
He laughed.

00:13:33.118 --> 00:13:36.650
Gromit looked at Wallace and the Penguin.

00:13:36.709 --> 00:13:40.151
and he felt angrier and angrier.

00:13:40.211 --> 00:13:44.384
That evening Grommet went out into the garden again.

00:13:44.444 --> 00:13:51.701
Through the window he could see Wallace and the penguin eating and drinking happily in the back room.

00:13:51.721 --> 00:13:54.724
A more cheese penguin?

00:13:54.784 --> 00:13:56.334
asked Wallace.

00:13:56.394 --> 00:13:59.608
Grommet looked away sadly.

00:13:59.668 --> 00:14:01.584
He went into his kennel.

00:14:01.644 --> 00:14:08.052
and put two or three of his most important things into a red and white bag.

00:14:08.112 --> 00:14:15.584
Before he left, he took an old photo of Wallace in his hands and looked at it for a minute or two.

00:14:15.644 --> 00:14:28.932
Then he put the photo down, put on his yellow coat and hat, put his bag on his back, and walked off into the rain.

00:14:28.992 --> 00:14:44.508
Under the cold rain, Grommet slowly walked away from his kennel, away from his home in West Wallaby Street, and away from his old friend, Wallace.

00:14:44.568 --> 00:14:50.992
From the house the penguin watched Grommet go, and was happy.

00:14:51.052 --> 00:14:57.448
Then he went off to find the techno trousers.

00:14:57.507 --> 00:15:05.292
The next morning Gromit got up early after a night sleeping in a bin in the street.

00:15:05.352 --> 00:15:10.954
At home in West Wallaby Street, Wallace was happy in his bed.

00:15:11.014 --> 00:15:14.026
He opened his eyes slowly.

00:15:14.086 --> 00:15:21.789
Just then the head of his bed moved up, and the door opened in the floor at the foot of the bed.

00:15:21.849 --> 00:15:34.477
Wallace shot out of bed, threw the door in the floor and down into the kitchen, But this time he didn't land in his usual brown trousers.

00:15:34.537 --> 00:15:38.500
He landed in the techno trousers.

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:41.752
They're the wrong trousers!

00:15:41.812 --> 00:15:42.693
He cried.

00:15:42.713 --> 00:15:45.646
Then the trousers moved.

00:15:45.706 --> 00:15:50.149
But there was no control panel on the front of them to stop them.

00:15:50.209 --> 00:15:52.901
Where's the control panel?

00:15:52.961 --> 00:15:54.222
cried Wallace.

00:15:54.282 --> 00:15:56.224
Stop them, Gromit!

00:15:56.284 --> 00:15:59.472
Get me out of these trousers!

00:15:59.532 --> 00:16:04.960
But Grommet wasn't there, and the techno-trousers didn't stop.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:11.514
They walked out of the front door and down the street with Wallace in them.

00:16:11.574 --> 00:16:15.877
Grommet looked at a sign in a shop-window.

00:16:15.938 --> 00:16:18.990
Spare room to rent.

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:21.422
Cheap, it said.

00:16:21.482 --> 00:16:23.202
Oh, good!

00:16:23.262 --> 00:16:24.384
he thought.

00:16:24.444 --> 00:16:25.924
He read more.

00:16:25.984 --> 00:16:27.996
No dogs.

00:16:28.056 --> 00:16:29.904
The sign went on.

00:16:29.964 --> 00:16:31.743
Oh, no!

00:16:31.802 --> 00:16:33.464
thought Grommet.

00:16:33.524 --> 00:16:37.808
Then he saw a picture of a chicken in the window.

00:16:37.868 --> 00:16:44.535
Help us to find this chicken, and you get one thousand pounds!"

00:16:44.595 --> 00:16:46.127
Grommet read.

00:16:46.186 --> 00:16:48.709
He looked at the picture carefully.

00:16:48.769 --> 00:16:52.079
Did he know that chicken's face?

00:16:52.139 --> 00:16:57.139
Just then, Wallace ran past in the techno-trousers.

00:16:57.199 --> 00:16:59.550
Help, Gromit!"

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:00.561
he cried.

00:17:00.621 --> 00:17:03.934
They're the wrong trousers!

00:17:03.994 --> 00:17:07.055
Gromit ran after his old friend.

00:17:07.075 --> 00:17:11.108
What's wrong with the techno-trousers?

00:17:11.168 --> 00:17:12.228
He thought.

00:17:12.289 --> 00:17:18.572
And then, in the street in front of him, he saw the penguin.

00:17:18.632 --> 00:17:21.064
What's he got there?

00:17:21.124 --> 00:17:22.658
Thought Gromit.

00:17:22.718 --> 00:17:27.513
quietly he moved nearer, and then he saw.

00:17:27.573 --> 00:17:31.096
The penguin had the control panel.

00:17:31.156 --> 00:17:33.718
Now grommet understood.

00:17:33.778 --> 00:17:45.706
With the buttons and levers, the penguin could make the techno-trousers move here and there, up and down, and Wallace couldn't stop him.

00:17:45.766 --> 00:17:49.998
In the end the techno-trousers took Wallace home.

00:17:50.058 --> 00:18:04.478
He felt very tired by then, Because he couldn't get out of the techno trousers, he went to bed in them and he went to sleep at once.

00:18:04.538 --> 00:18:09.554
CHAPTER IV.

00:18:09.614 --> 00:18:18.842
WATCHING AND WAITING Grommet was in a coffee shop.

00:18:18.902 --> 00:18:25.346
He looked over his newspaper at the street, and saw the penguin walking past.

00:18:25.406 --> 00:18:34.514
He quickly put his newspaper down, left some money for his coffee on the table, and went out into the street after the penguin.

00:18:34.574 --> 00:18:39.218
Soon the penguin stopped in front of a big old building.

00:18:39.278 --> 00:18:41.990
What's he doing here?

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:43.570
thought Gromit.

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:46.865
Suddenly the penguin looked behind him.

00:18:46.925 --> 00:18:50.680
Grommet quickly hid behind some bins.

00:18:50.740 --> 00:18:59.286
Then the penguin looked back at the big old building and began writing lots of things down in a little book.

00:18:59.346 --> 00:19:06.232
Grommet got under an old box and moved slowly nearer to the old building.

00:19:06.292 --> 00:19:08.354
But how could he see out now?

00:19:08.374 --> 00:19:09.523
Easy!

00:19:09.583 --> 00:19:17.878
He took out a little red knife, made a hole in the front of the box, and looked carefully through it.

00:19:17.938 --> 00:19:22.371
Now the penguin had a yellow tape measure in his hand.

00:19:22.431 --> 00:19:26.264
First he looked up at a high window over his head.

00:19:26.324 --> 00:19:34.340
After that he made his tape measure very long, and put one end of it up on the ledge in front of the high window.

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:43.841
And then, when the other end of the tape measure went up, The penguin shot up with it and landed on the high window ledge.

00:19:43.901 --> 00:19:50.563
Up there, on the ledge, the penguin looked at the big window in front of him carefully.

00:19:50.623 --> 00:20:01.518
He measured it from left to right and up and down, and he wrote lots more things down in his little book.

00:20:01.578 --> 00:20:10.154
When he finished writing, he put his book under his arm, and he put one end of the tape measure on the window ledge again.

00:20:10.214 --> 00:20:18.525
And then, when the other end of the tape measure went down, the penguin came down with it and landed in the street.

00:20:18.585 --> 00:20:21.876
He began walking past Gromit's box.

00:20:21.936 --> 00:20:27.141
Suddenly he stopped and looked right at the box.

00:20:27.201 --> 00:20:28.786
Oh, no!

00:20:28.846 --> 00:20:30.996
He knows I'm in here!"

00:20:31.056 --> 00:20:35.288
thought Gromit, and he watched and waited.

00:20:35.348 --> 00:20:41.710
But in the end the penguin only looked at the box for a minute and then walked on.

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:50.638
Soon after that, Gromit came out from under the box and ran back to 62 West Wallaby Street.

00:20:50.698 --> 00:20:58.586
He got there before the penguin, and at once went upstairs into his old room, now the penguin's room.

00:20:58.646 --> 00:21:03.079
He found something very interesting on the penguin's table.

00:21:03.139 --> 00:21:09.722
It was a picture of the big old building, and all the different rooms in it.

00:21:09.782 --> 00:21:23.217
It was the town museum, and there In the diamond room on the second floor, not far from the window, was a big, blue diamond.

00:21:23.277 --> 00:21:25.318
Of course!

00:21:25.378 --> 00:21:26.889
Thought Grommet.

00:21:26.949 --> 00:21:31.872
The penguin wants to get the blue diamond from the museum.

00:21:31.932 --> 00:21:36.945
Just then, he heard the back door open and close.

00:21:37.005 --> 00:21:38.456
Oh no!

00:21:38.516 --> 00:21:40.427
The penguin's back!

00:21:40.487 --> 00:21:41.828
Thought Grommet!

00:21:41.888 --> 00:21:44.224
Where can I hide now?

00:21:44.284 --> 00:21:46.850
There was no time to run away.

00:21:46.910 --> 00:21:51.294
So in the end, Gromit hid in bed, next to Wallace.

00:21:51.354 --> 00:21:57.538
When he looked out, he saw the penguin bringing a big box into Wallace's room.

00:21:57.598 --> 00:22:05.504
Then the penguin put the box down, and Gromit saw the red glove on his head.

00:22:05.564 --> 00:22:10.698
At once he remembered the picture of the chicken in the shop window.

00:22:10.758 --> 00:22:13.878
So he's the chicken.

00:22:13.938 --> 00:22:17.428
thought grommet, and he hid again quickly.

00:22:17.488 --> 00:22:24.172
Now the penguin took a red helmet out of the box and put it on Wallace's head.

00:22:24.232 --> 00:22:27.874
Wallace slept happily through this.

00:22:27.934 --> 00:22:38.291
With the control panel of the techno trousers, the penguin made Wallace get out of bed, walk downstairs, and leave the house.

00:22:38.351 --> 00:22:41.625
Wallace slept through all this.

00:22:41.686 --> 00:22:47.272
and the penguin walked down the street after him to the town museum.

00:22:47.332 --> 00:22:53.636
At the same time, back in Wallace's room, the getting up machine began working.

00:22:53.696 --> 00:23:01.913
The head of the bed moved up, the door opened in the floor at its foot, and grommet shot down through it.

00:23:01.973 --> 00:23:13.768
He landed in Wallace's brown trousers, at the kitchen table, and there he got breakfast all over his face.

00:23:13.828 --> 00:23:18.316
Chapter 5.

00:23:18.376 --> 00:23:24.039
Hoops and Downs.

00:23:24.099 --> 00:23:35.786
Wallace and the penguin walked through the dark streets to the museum, and Wallace didn't open his eyes once.

00:23:35.846 --> 00:23:41.968
When they arrived at the museum, the penguin moved some levers on the control panel.

00:23:42.028 --> 00:23:49.868
Then he jumped up on the techno trousers, and at once they began to walk up the wall of the museum.

00:23:49.928 --> 00:23:58.101
Soon the trousers arrived at the high window, and here the penguin jumped off and landed on the window ledge.

00:23:58.161 --> 00:24:06.424
He looked through the window at the beautiful blue diamond and moved some more levers on the control panel.

00:24:06.484 --> 00:24:14.624
The techno trousers went higher up the wall with wallace in them, At last they arrived at the roof.

00:24:14.684 --> 00:24:26.991
There they walked up, over and down an air vent, through the roof and down into the museum, and Wallace slept through it all.

00:24:27.052 --> 00:24:31.865
Now the penguin could see the techno trousers through the window.

00:24:31.925 --> 00:24:35.706
They came down through an air vent in the ceiling.

00:24:35.766 --> 00:24:43.572
walked over the ceiling tiles in the long room, and came nearer and nearer to the diamond room.

00:24:43.632 --> 00:24:49.346
But Wallace had long arms, and the penguin suddenly felt afraid.

00:24:49.406 --> 00:24:58.092
Those long arms could easily get in front of the alarm and make it ring, so he stopped the trousers for a time.

00:24:58.152 --> 00:25:02.198
In the end, Wallace moved his arms in his sleep.

00:25:02.258 --> 00:25:09.176
and the penguin quickly moved some levers on the control panel and walked him past the alarm.

00:25:09.236 --> 00:25:12.498
Now the diamond was under him.

00:25:12.558 --> 00:25:25.077
Then the penguin hit a button on the control panel and the red helmet on Wallace's head opened and a steel machine claw came down out of it.

00:25:25.138 --> 00:25:31.978
After that the penguin hit a different button and moved some of the levers on the control panel.

00:25:32.038 --> 00:25:40.971
The trousers moved, and the machine claw went down to the diamond, and opened over it.

00:25:41.031 --> 00:25:48.586
Now the steel claw closed on the diamond, and the penguin hit some more buttons.

00:25:48.646 --> 00:25:56.602
The claw, with the diamond in it, slowly began to go up into Wallace's helmet.

00:25:56.663 --> 00:26:06.600
Then, suddenly, the diamond shot out of the claw, At once the penguin moved the lever and hit a button.

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:13.714
The steel claw shot down and closed on the diamond again before it hit the floor.

00:26:13.774 --> 00:26:22.408
Once again the penguin hit some more buttons and the claw moved up into the helmet with the diamond in it.

00:26:22.468 --> 00:26:25.060
Then it happened.

00:26:25.120 --> 00:26:28.622
One of the ceiling tiles came off the ceiling.

00:26:28.682 --> 00:26:32.965
and with it came one of the feet of the techno-trousers.

00:26:33.025 --> 00:26:41.808
At the same time the helmet opened again, and the steel claw with the diamond in moved down in front of the alarm.

00:26:41.868 --> 00:26:44.470
The alarm began to ring.

00:26:44.530 --> 00:26:47.851
Lights began to go on and off.

00:26:47.911 --> 00:26:50.552
Wallace opened his eyes.

00:26:50.612 --> 00:26:52.083
Where am I?

00:26:52.143 --> 00:26:54.064
What's that noise?

00:26:54.124 --> 00:26:55.346
He cried.

00:26:55.406 --> 00:27:00.650
At the same time a big steel door closed in front of him.

00:27:00.711 --> 00:27:05.274
How could the penguin get the diamond out of the museum now?

00:27:05.334 --> 00:27:09.886
The air vent was in the long room behind the steel door.

00:27:09.946 --> 00:27:11.237
Grummit!

00:27:11.297 --> 00:27:13.158
Grummit!

00:27:13.219 --> 00:27:14.610
cried Wallace.

00:27:14.670 --> 00:27:20.023
The penguin hit some buttons and moved some levers on the control panel.

00:27:20.083 --> 00:27:24.971
The techno trousers walked to the window and stood on it.

00:27:25.032 --> 00:27:34.916
At once the window opened, and Wallace was out in the cold, standing on a high window, looking up at the night sky.

00:27:34.976 --> 00:27:40.622
Now the trousers moved, and he could see the dark street under him.

00:27:40.683 --> 00:27:43.475
Get me down!

00:27:43.535 --> 00:27:44.696
cried Wallace.

00:27:44.756 --> 00:27:46.470
Help!

00:27:46.529 --> 00:27:55.116
Then the penguin jumped on Wallace's back, and the techno-trousers quickly walked down the wall and ran away.

00:27:55.136 --> 00:27:58.678
You can't do this to me!

00:27:58.738 --> 00:27:59.989
cried Wallace.

00:28:00.049 --> 00:28:02.150
Stop it at once!

00:28:02.210 --> 00:28:07.923
I'm a good man I am!

00:28:07.984 --> 00:28:25.556
Chapter 6 Be Careful Land The penguin took Wallace back to his room at 62 West Wallaby Street.

00:28:25.616 --> 00:28:29.897
There, Wallace took off the helmet and put it down.

00:28:29.957 --> 00:28:34.958
There, too, the penguin took the red glove off his head.

00:28:35.018 --> 00:28:46.938
Oh, it's you, said Wallace, for he saw now it wasn't a chicken standing in front of him, but the penguin Then he got angry.

00:28:46.998 --> 00:28:50.631
Get me out of these trousers this minute!"

00:28:50.691 --> 00:28:51.882
he said.

00:28:51.942 --> 00:28:59.047
In answer, the penguin quickly put Wallace into a wardrobe and closed the door behind him.

00:28:59.107 --> 00:29:00.348
Help!

00:29:00.408 --> 00:29:02.639
Open this door at once!

00:29:02.699 --> 00:29:07.652
cried Wallace in the wardrobe, and he knocked on the door angrily.

00:29:07.712 --> 00:29:12.966
The penguin took the diamond from the helmet and put it in a bag.

00:29:13.026 --> 00:29:15.284
Then he walked to the door.

00:29:15.344 --> 00:29:18.110
But Gromit stood at the door.

00:29:18.170 --> 00:29:23.043
He was angry, and he had a big rolling pin in his hands.

00:29:23.103 --> 00:29:27.145
At once the penguin took out a big black gun.

00:29:27.205 --> 00:29:30.967
When he saw that, Gromit put his rolling pin down.

00:29:31.027 --> 00:29:34.319
Now the penguin opened the wardrobe door.

00:29:34.379 --> 00:29:39.172
Gromit got in with Wallace, and the penguin closed the door again.

00:29:39.232 --> 00:29:45.739
In the dark, Gromit began to put his hands down the front of the techno trousers.

00:29:45.799 --> 00:29:48.764
What are you doing, cried Wallace?

00:29:48.824 --> 00:29:50.954
Be careful, Land!"

00:29:51.014 --> 00:30:03.808
Gromit put the end of a red wire on the end of a black wire, and the legs of the techno-trousers began to move up and down, faster and faster.

00:30:03.868 --> 00:30:12.805
Soon the wardrobe broke away from the floor, and the trousers walked it out of the room with Wallace and Gromit in it.

00:30:12.865 --> 00:30:14.591
Where are we going?

00:30:14.611 --> 00:30:17.232
I can't see a thing!"

00:30:17.292 --> 00:30:18.764
cried Wallace.

00:30:18.824 --> 00:30:23.086
Then the wardrobe door opened and Gromit came out.

00:30:23.146 --> 00:30:31.212
The penguin jumped on the banister and went down it with the gun in his hand and the diamond bag on his back.

00:30:31.272 --> 00:30:34.984
He landed on the front of Wallace's toy train.

00:30:35.004 --> 00:30:37.246
"'Get him, Gromit!"

00:30:37.306 --> 00:30:40.001
cried Wallace from in the wardrobe.

00:30:40.061 --> 00:30:44.577
Then the wardrobe began to go downstairs with Wallace in it.

00:30:44.638 --> 00:30:48.970
Gromit jumped up at once and caught the ceiling lamp.

00:30:49.030 --> 00:30:59.326
The penguin shot the lamp down from the ceiling and Gromit landed near the back of Wallace's toy train with the lamp on his head.

00:30:59.386 --> 00:31:03.729
The train went off quickly down the track.

00:31:03.789 --> 00:31:09.094
The penguin was now behind the little blue train engine.

00:31:09.154 --> 00:31:14.238
He looked back, and shot at Gromit again and again with his gun.

00:31:14.298 --> 00:31:16.789
But Gromit wasn't afraid.

00:31:16.849 --> 00:31:22.662
He had a lamp for a helmet on his head, and he wanted to catch the penguin.

00:31:22.722 --> 00:31:27.435
Suddenly, he saw the train getting near the back door.

00:31:27.495 --> 00:31:28.786
Oh, no!

00:31:28.846 --> 00:31:31.357
The penguin's going to get away!

00:31:31.418 --> 00:31:32.478
He thought.

00:31:32.538 --> 00:31:37.847
He hit a red button by the track, and the train went off to the left.

00:31:37.907 --> 00:31:40.054
It's okay, Gromit!"

00:31:40.114 --> 00:31:41.354
cried Wallace.

00:31:41.414 --> 00:31:48.317
He now stood on the last car, at the end of the train, on one leg of the techno-trousers.

00:31:48.377 --> 00:31:50.398
I'm behind you, lad!

00:31:50.458 --> 00:31:51.628
He called.

00:31:51.688 --> 00:32:02.253
Now the penguin shot his gun at Wallace's feet, and Wallace's car jumped off the track, and began to run on a new track next to the first.

00:32:02.313 --> 00:32:04.344
Stay there, Gromit!

00:32:04.404 --> 00:32:07.072
Everything's okay!

00:32:07.132 --> 00:32:12.431
and he moved past his friend and got near the penguin.

00:32:12.491 --> 00:32:14.852
Give me that gun!'

00:32:14.912 --> 00:32:16.173
cried Wallace.

00:32:16.232 --> 00:32:30.939
He put out his hand and took the gun from the penguin, but suddenly the techno-trousers hit the wall and Wallace came out of them, went through a hole in the wall and landed on a kitchen trolley.

00:32:30.999 --> 00:32:37.550
At once Grommet took the lamp off his head and began to move to the front of the train.

00:32:37.610 --> 00:32:39.841
Wallace went past him again.

00:32:39.861 --> 00:32:45.736
This time he was on his trolley, and he had a net in his hands.

00:32:45.796 --> 00:32:49.680
I'm going to get that penguin now, he cried.

00:32:49.740 --> 00:32:56.158
But then Wallace's net hit something on the wall, and this knocked him off the trolley.

00:32:56.218 --> 00:32:58.450
He landed back on the train.

00:32:58.510 --> 00:33:02.098
The penguin hit a little lever by the track.

00:33:02.158 --> 00:33:08.100
The engine, with the penguin on a car behind it, went off along one track.

00:33:08.160 --> 00:33:17.118
The back of the train, with Gromit on the first car, and Wallace on the last car, went off along a different track.

00:33:17.178 --> 00:33:22.374
Suddenly, Gromit had no more track in front of him.

00:33:22.434 --> 00:33:23.745
Oh, no!

00:33:23.805 --> 00:33:27.229
We're going to have an accident, he thought.

00:33:27.289 --> 00:33:36.772
Then he saw a box of new track on the floor, caught it, and quickly began to put the new track down in front of the train.

00:33:36.832 --> 00:33:42.324
So they went on, under the table, and into the next room.

00:33:42.384 --> 00:33:46.585
There Gromit's track ran over the penguins' track.

00:33:46.645 --> 00:33:55.362
At the back of the train, Wallace put out his hands to catch the penguin, but he only caught the little blue toy engine.

00:33:55.422 --> 00:34:07.476
Then the techno trousers walked in front of the penguin's car and the penguin, with the diamond bag on his back, flew up, off the car and into the kitchen.

00:34:07.536 --> 00:34:13.383
At the same time, grommet hit the kitchen cupboard and stopped suddenly.

00:34:13.443 --> 00:34:18.398
A milk bottle came down off the cupboard and landed in his hand.

00:34:18.418 --> 00:34:26.784
A second later, the penguin landed in the milk bottle, and the diamond bag landed in Gromit's other hand.

00:34:26.804 --> 00:34:29.756
We did it, Gromit Land!

00:34:29.816 --> 00:34:31.677
We caught him!"

00:34:31.737 --> 00:34:33.507
cried Wallace.

00:34:33.568 --> 00:34:45.310
That afternoon they took the penguin to the police, and the police put him away in a very strong building for a very long time.

00:34:45.370 --> 00:34:49.871
That evening Wallis and Gromit sat in the front room.

00:34:49.932 --> 00:34:52.162
They were friends again.

00:34:52.222 --> 00:34:56.413
Now we've got the thousand pounds from the police.

00:34:56.473 --> 00:34:59.314
We don't need to rent that spare room.

00:34:59.374 --> 00:35:02.745
Isn't that grand, said Wallis happily?

00:35:02.805 --> 00:35:05.795
Shall we have some cheese, Chuck?"

00:35:05.856 --> 00:35:15.648
When Grommet got up to get the cheese, he looked out of the window at the old techno trousers, now in a bin in the street.

00:35:15.708 --> 00:35:20.839
And we don't need you, he thought happily.

00:35:20.899 --> 00:35:28.191
He went back into the front room with Wallace's cheese, and then sat down to read the newspaper.

00:35:28.251 --> 00:35:37.474
Out in the street, with no control panel to stop them, The techno trousers got up and walked off into the night.

